think The two parents confirmed the roundness reconciliation is genuinely deferrable, not a clean one-lap close: inscribed_disk reports radius in chamfer 3-4 units (a 5x5 block reads inradius 3.0) while min_enclosing_circle reports true Euclidean (the same block reads circumradius 2.828), so a naive inradius<=circumradius really flips on a compact square. Reconciling wants a shared continuous convention (doubled-integer pixel-square coordinates) -- real work, honestly deferred again.
think Crux-first among tractable options: the sharper, still-tractable crux the family has NARRATED for a dozen rungs yet never MEASURED is topology. Block-versus-ring recurs across contour and inscribed_disk (identical outer contour, hull, enclosing circle) -- but no rung COUNTS the hole. The Euler number does it, exact-integer (pure counting, no float, no tolerance), the family's signature virtue kept.
think Built image/euler_number.rye: the Euler number (components - holes) by BIT-QUAD counting (S.B. Gray 1971). Slide a 2x2 window over the region with a one-pixel background border, tally Q1 (one foreground pixel, an outer corner), Q3 (three, an inner corner), QD (a diagonal two, a corner-touch pinch); for the 8-connected foreground image/label.rye uses, E = (Q1 - Q3 - 2*QD) / 4, a theorem whose numerator is always a multiple of four. A single labeled region is one 8-connected component, so components = 1 and holes = 1 - E.
think Designed the decisive cruxes before coding, then let metal prove the convention rather than memory. GREEN on the FIRST full run, no reds: a solid 5x5 block reads Euler 1 (no hole), a hollow 5x5 ring Euler 0 (one hole) though their outer bounds are byte-for-byte identical -- topology sees the hole the convex readers cannot and inscribed_disk only hinted with a shrunken depth; a plus and a ring are BOTH dented (shape_signature reads solidity below one for each), so solidity merges them, yet the plus has no hole (Euler 1) and the ring one (Euler 0) -- the Euler number the axis that separates a pair solidity collapses, orthogonal to it; a 5x9 block pierced twice reads Euler -1 (two holes), the count running negative and staying exact.
obs Verified the 8-connected bit-quad sign convention by hand on two tiny cases before trusting it (single pixel: Q1=4 -> E=1; two diagonal pixels: Q1=6, QD=1 -> E_8=1 one component, E_4=2 two -- confirming 8-connected wants -2*QD and matches label.rye's connectivity so component counts here and there always agree). Metal then confirmed block 1, ring 0, plus 1, two-hole -1 -- measurement over memory.
obs Refuses BadLabel (a label of zero or past the component count), having tallied nothing; determinism proven. Compose not braid -- owns only the bit-quad sweep and the reads (hole_count, is_simply_connected, has_hole); label owns the component map and its 8-connectivity, qoi the pixel ceiling. No hull, no distance field, no pixel written -- a reading, not a render.
